## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine multiple auth standards (OIDC, SAML) with a per-request binding mechanism, a realistic replay-protection pattern, and per-tenant isolation.

## Key Concepts
- OIDC ID tokens and SAML assertions as inputs
- Internal JWT with tenant, aud, scopes and fingerprint binding
- Replay protection via per-token fingerprint cache
- OpenAPI security schema for internal tokens
- SAML-to-claims adapter mapping SAML to standard claims

## Code Example
```javascript
// Issuance sketch (pseudo)
function issueInternalJwt(userClaims, fingerprint) {
  const payload = { ...userClaims, fingerprint, iat: now(), exp: nowPlus(300) }
  return signJwt(payload, gatewayPrivateKey)
}
```

```javascript
// Verification sketch (pseudo)
function verifyInternalJwt(token, fingerprint) {
  const payload = verifyJwt(token, gatewayPublicKey)
  return payload.fingerprint === fingerprint && payload.exp > now()
}
```

